{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"justjack420","id":"592252026226999306","is_bot":0,"username":"justjack420"},"author_id":"592252026226999306","channel_id":"747915178187817123","content":"**Fae'd Oak** (Ferrytown)- Weapons or Armor made from this wyld wood have no metal within them, but are just as sturdy as their metal counterparts. Armor made from this Fae'd Oak gives resistance to Psychic and Force Damage. Weapons carved from Fae'd Oak are much less common, mainly because of their instability, when you Crit with these weapons roll on the Fae'd Oak wild magic table.\n\n1- Sap pours from the palm of your hands and hardens around whatever weapon you are wielding. For the next 10 minutes the weapon deals an extra damage die of force damage on the first attack that hits and you cannot be disarmed and not use whatever hand or hands are stuck to the weapon.\n\n2- The latent Fae magic in the weapon surges from within it and into you, revitalizing your stamina. You can roll a d6+2 or a d8+2 and gain that number of hit points or temporary hit points, respectively.\n\n3- A flumph appears in an empty location of your choosing within 30 feet of you. It, startled at both the sudden atomization and deatomization, uses its Stench Spray ability and disappears at the start of your next turn.\n\n4- Large vines and roots grow out of the weapon, wrapping around you, and planting themselves into the ground surrounding you. For the next minute or until you take 20 damage the ground 10 feet within you becomes difficult terrain, you gain +2 AC, and resistance to bludgeoning, piercing, and slashing damage.","created_at":"2021-02-04T00:41:40.310000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"806685875886096425","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
